<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01VY">Remark <span data-tag="01VY">5.2.5.4</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a cocartesian fibration of simplicial sets, and let $\operatorname{hTr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ be the homotopy transport representation of Construction <a data-tag="019U" href="/tag/019U">5.2.5.2</a>. It follows from Proposition <a data-tag="01UM" href="/tag/01UM">5.1.4.15</a> that $U$ is a left fibration if and only if the functor $\operatorname{hTr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ factors through the full subcategory $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}} \subseteq \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$. In particular, if $U$ is a left fibration, then Construction <a data-tag="019U" href="/tag/019U">5.2.5.2</a> determines a functor $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ which we will also refer to as the <em>homotopy transport representation</em> of the left fibration $U$. </p>
